#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""box — your view of this shared machine.

  box status [--agent|--json]      usage, limits, box load, pending deletions
  box ports                        your port range (+ which are in use)
  box heavy -- CMD...              run a heavy job: queued, low priority, capped parallelism
  box serve add NAME [--port P] -- CMD...   long-running server (survives logout/reboot)
  box serve ls | logs NAME | restart NAME | stop NAME | start NAME | rm NAME
  box shared ls | create NAME | set NAME [--port P] -- CMD... | start|stop|restart|rm NAME | logs NAME [-n N]
                                   servers the whole group owns (code in /srv/shared/NAME); add --json
  box clean [--dry-run]            clean caches/old tmp/idle build outputs now
  box restore [NAME]               put an archived project back in ~/projects (lists archives without NAME)
  box rules                        the rules your agents are given
  box t3 [pair|status|stop|logs]   your own T3 Code web UI: start it and get a pairing link
  box setup [--check]              guided setup: git identity, GitHub, agent logins
  box agents                       installed coding agents + whether you're logged in
  box updates [auto|manual|now]    whether your coding agents update daily (status without an argument)
  box request "TEXT"               ask the owner for something (e.g. a system package)
  box issue [--kind K] "TEXT"      log something that slowed you down or didn't work (agents do this)
  box issues [--days N] [--json]   what's been logged in ~/.sharedbox/issues.jsonl
"""

